  "showTitle": "The Hard Saying",
  "title": "Out Loud",
  "dates": "Sunday, November 22 – Wednesday, November 25, 2009",
  "logline": "A correction sent after a morning of drafts, a reply that takes all day, a grandmother on the stairs — and coffee at an hour nobody keeps, the night before everyone goes home.",
  "previously": [
    {
      "text": "In Montecito a girl in a window seat had Flannery O’Connor exactly backwards. You crossed the room yourself.",
      "if": "met_skye"
    },
    {
      "text": "Soaking wet on the sand at Ellery Beach: “I’d like to kiss you now.”",
      "if": "kissed_skye"
    },
    {
      "text": "She typed herself into your phone — SKYE (MISFIT). You asked her last name. “Out.”",
      "if": "skye_has_number"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the basement Lena played “Clair de lune” properly, around the dead F. “The last time I played it right in front of anybody was in November. Four years ago.”",
      "if": "knows_lena_piano_played"
    },
    {
      "text": "At halftime you asked Theo home to Youngstown. He said yes before you finished, and bought two tickets to Pittsburgh. “Guests bring something.”",
      "if": "theo_youngstown && theo_paid_flights"
    },
    {
      "text": "Theo: “Where’d you go?” “Walked home.” “From *Montecito*.”",
      "if": "jack_lied_theo_skye"
    },
    {
      "text": "You came home at six in the morning, soaked and humming, and wouldn’t tell Theo where you’d been.",
      "if": "met_skye && !jack_lied_theo_skye"
    }
  ],
